@F25 @visual-direction
Feature: Compose a thoughtful visual narrative by construction

  Scenario: Turn one audience-state change into a coherent staged beat
    Given a beat names its audience question, single takeaway, hero, visual metaphor, and semantic transition
    And the storyboard identifies any context the viewer must keep recognizing
    And the project defines role-based typography, motion, safe regions, a caption lane, and a maximum active-object budget
    When the director authors the beat with DirectedScene
    Then the hero is the only primary focus and retained context is visibly subordinate
    And independent elements receive non-overlapping stage placements without covering the caption lane
    And text uses semantic type roles rather than per-object styling or unreadable shrinking
    And motion expresses continuation, contrast, reveal, or chapter transitions consistently
    And the final visual state makes the declared takeaway inferable without a pile of explanatory cards
